  "bio": "Qin received the M.F.A. degree in information arts and design from Tsinghua University, China, in 2016. Her research area includes human-computer interaction, user experience, and accessibility. Her PhD research focuses on using interactive technologies to help children with autism, especially in daily activities learning and social skills improve. She is also the lab director and leads the Interactive Media Studio .\n\nQin grew up in Sichuan, China. In her spare time, she enjoys playing guitar and football.",
